## Retro Notes & Adjustments
<!-- ID: retro_notes -->
- Research was sufficient for architecture because the critical seams were verified directly in source before planning.
- The first implementation slice should not add caching, inline suppressions, or extra public actions unless validation later proves they are necessary.
- If parser evaluation fails for both candidates, implementation must fall back to the same interface contract rather than reopening architecture with a replacement system.
